From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pyo <pyo@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:17:19 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat: make the object key prefix of backups configurable

Backups are stored under "moco/<namespace>/<name>/" in the bucket.
Add bucketConfig.prefix (moco-backup --prefix) to store them under
"<prefix>/<namespace>/<name>/" instead, e.g. to keep several tenants'
backups apart in one bucket.  It defaults to "moco", so nothing
changes unless it is set.  A restore reads the backups from the same
place, using its own jobConfig.bucketConfig.prefix.
